assertion  XSH.iswgraph.001
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswgraph() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class graph as the locale definition lists it: the letters,
           the digits and the 32 punctuation characters.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswgraph.002
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswgraph() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the space and the control characters.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswgraph.003
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswgraph(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswgraph.004
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each of the 128 characters, iswgraph() is non-zero exactly when
           iswprint() is non-zero and the character is not the space; and also
           exactly when iswalnum() or iswpunct() is non-zero.
test       t/004-graph-is-print-but-space.c

assertion  XSH.iswgraph.005
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswgraph.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale, iswgraph() is non-zero for the letters and
           digits and 0 for the space.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
